Subject: [PATCH] Persian/RTL fixes, accessibility, UX and SEO improvements
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stage 1 (Persian and accessibility)
- Persian font fallback in all display text; reset letter-spacing for fa only
- Logo isolated as LTR (lang=en) so the orange dot keeps its place in RTL
- Persian digits in fa mode (section numbers, counts, years, footer Jalali year)
- Exhibition dialog: focus move/trap/return, inert background, scroll lock
- Language button names the target language; labels translated
- Text colors raised to WCAG AA (muted, orange-text, CTA, status)

Stage 2 (structure and UX)
- Skip link, :focus-visible styles, Education h2, grouped city buttons
- Decorative arrows aria-hidden and mirrored in RTL
- Research added to nav; all links visible on mobile (scrollable second row)
- Persian city names and exhibition dialog content
- Thesis year shown as 2017 (en) / 1396 (fa)

Stage 3 (SEO, content, performance)
- Persist language; per-language title/description/og/twitter tags
- Open Graph, Twitter Card, canonical, JSON-LD, robots.txt, sitemap.xml
- Non-link project rows no longer look clickable
- CV button prepared via CV_URL constant (no fake link)
- Reveal CSS added; hero uses svh; numbering 01/07 matches 7 sections
- "ROMANTIC SENSIBILITY" Persian label changed to «نگاه رمانتیک»
